Hi there,

**Describe the bug**

If a UDP package is sent out using `zsock_send` and the length of the frame on the wire is a multiple of 64 Byte (128, 192, or 256, and so on) the package is not transmitted. Instead the package seems to be buffered. Next calls of `zsock_send` seem also to be buffered, until the sum of all the buffered data is no multiple of 64 Bytes. Then the first package is sent out and all the other data appears in the ethernet trailer. At least it looks like that in Wireshark.

**To Reproduce**

Sniff with wireshark on USB. Do something like the following code on the MCU.

```c
static char my_63_data[21];
static char my_64_data[22/*+64*/];
static struct sockaddr dst_addr;
static int sock_fd;

void some_init()
{
	/* set some dst_addr */
	/*...*/

	zsock_socket(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, IPPROTO_UDP);
	zsock_connect(sock_fd, dst_addr, sizeof(struct sockaddr_in));
	int flags = zsock_fcntl(sock_fd, F_GETFL, 0);
	zsock_fcntl(sock_fd, F_SETFL, flags | O_NONBLOCK);

	snprintf(&my_63_data, sizeof(my_63_data), "63B 63B 63B 63B 63B ");
	snprintf(&my_64_data, sizeof(my_64_data), "64B 64B 64B 64B 64B 4");
}

void send_64_byte(void)
{
	zsock_send(sock_fd, &my_64_data, sizeof(my_64_data), 0);
}

void send_63_byte(void)
{
	zsock_send(sock_fd, &my_63_data, sizeof(my_63_data), 0);
}
```

Call the functions `send_63_byte` and `send_64_byte` several times in some random order.


**Expected behavior**
For each zsock_send call a frame in wireshark.

**Impact**
Some packages get dropped, if the application waits for a response it will timeout eventually or wait forever.

**Logs and console output**
![grafik](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/assets/32814338/88b0aefe-085e-4225-bcd7-0fb25c2cda6c)
The "+64" in the example has been uncommented, that's why the payload longer and filled with more zeros. Then `send_63_byte`, `send_64_byte`, and `send_63_byte` have been called in this order.


**Environment**

I use Zephyr OS @ a8a0eb52439caccf51c66f845b2c29ceef0da39e on an STM32H730VB MCU with a gcc-arm-none-eabi-10.3-2021.07 toolchain.

Relevant config:
```
CONFIG_NETWORKING=y
CONFIG_NET_IPV6=n
CONFIG_NET_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NET_UDP=y

CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_STACK_NEXT=y
CONFIG_NET_L2_ETHERNET=y
CONFIG_USBD_CDC_ECM_CLASS=y

CONFIG_NET_SOCKETS=y
```

**Additional context**
N/A

